<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48276" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thȳni</span></b> , ōrum,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θυνοί,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Thracian
			people</i>, <i>who emigrated to Bithynia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 11,
				18, § 41</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 32, 43, §
			150</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cat. 25, 7</span></i>.— Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thȳnus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Thyni</i>, <i>Thynian;</i>
			<b>poet.</b> for <i>Bithynian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">merx,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 7, 3</span></i>
			 (for which: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bithyna negotia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Ep. 1, 6, 33</span></i>
			).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thȳ-nĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., <i>the seat of
				the Thyni in Bithynia</i>, <i><span class="en">Cat. 31,
			5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thȳnĭăcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>Thyniac</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sinus,</span>”
				i. e. <i>of the Euxine in Thrace</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 1, 10, 35</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>D.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thȳnĭăs</span></b> ,
				ădis, <i>adj. f.</i>,
				<i>Thynian;</i>
			<b>poet.</b> for <i>Bithynian</i>:
			grata domus Nymphis umida Thyniasin (dat. Graec.),
				<i><span class="en">Prop. 1, 20, 34</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">id. 1, 20,
				12</span></i>, Dryasin, and <i><span class="en">id. 1, 20,
				32</span></i>, Hamadryasin).— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>E.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thȳnĭcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Bithynian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anulus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 19, 32</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lima,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Anthol. Lat. 2, p. 412</span></i>
			 Burm.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
